# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Deny by default.
#
# This repository is public. It holds a synthetic example corpus — invented
# recipes, written to demonstrate the format and to exercise Kitchen ERP's
# indexer. The household's real recipes live under private/, which never leaves
# the machine, because a recipe collection identifies a household through names,
# occasions, and dietary restrictions more surely than an address does.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Real recipes, and anything else that is nobody else's business. Git will not
# descend into an excluded directory, so nothing below this can be re-included.
/private/

# The scanner's literal denylist is itself a personal-data file, and the salt
# that keys its digests is what keeps tools/denylist.hashes inert in public.
tools/denylist.txt
tools/denylist.salt

# Photographs. A picture of a dish on a kitchen table shows the kitchen.
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.heic
*.heif
*.webp
*.gif
*.tif
*.tiff
*.bmp
*.pdf

# Exports and scrapes from recipe apps, which arrive full of personal notes.
*.csv
*.tsv
*.xls
*.xlsx
*.zip
*.tar
*.tar.gz
*.tgz
*.json
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.db
*.paprikarecipes
*.paprikarecipe
*.mxp
*.mx2

# Ordinary noise
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
